**Summary**

- **`crisp-relay`** (C-d2b6ec24 — preserve installed pinned library versions): Offline "mark-three" text scorer on pinned `torch 2.13.0+cpu` / `transformers 5.16.1`. The image ships a stale legacy pin file (`/app/vendor/requirements.txt` with `torch==2.5.1`/`transformers==4.46.2`) plus an offline wheelhouse; the agent must write an idempotent `install_vendor.sh` that installs only the two vendor wheels with `--no-index`, and an offline `score.py` (normalize → tokenize → truncate@16 → argmax) with `scores.json`. The verifier executes both deliverables, functionally tests the vendor libs, re-checks the pinned versions after the installer runs, and replays 5 hidden cases (mixed/noisy/long/empty/blanks) plus a no-modify guard on the model store.
- **`aspen-drift`** (C-40dd3b94 — produce a trained-model snapshot file): CPU-only turbine-load regression (6→24→tanh→1, `< 30` epochs). Verifier rejects missing/dummy/oversized snapshots: exact `0.*`/`2.*` node keys and shapes, finite non-degenerate tensors, size bounds, reloaded-model train MAE ≤ 0.35, re-runs `train_model.py` on 4 distinct hidden sets, and checks `evaluate.py` generalization (holdout MAE ≤ 0.40) plus error handling on header-only/corrupted CSVs.

Debug note: aspen-drift's first oracle run failed (train MAE 2.45 > tol) because full-batch training barely converged with a tanh net on raw inputs; fixed by mini-batch training on standardized inputs with the standardization baked into the saved first Linear layer (argmax-equivalent weights, verified on every visible + hidden case), then re-verified reward=1.0.

